ent-MobPirateT1MonkeyKnuckleDusters = boarding monkey
    .desc = The cheapest rookie on the crew. Will do anything for a paycheck in bananas. Wields brass knuckles bearing a blood-red S.
ent-MobPirateT1MonkeyFlareGun = gunner monkey
    .desc = The cheapest rookie on the crew. Will do anything for a paycheck in bananas. Armed with a flare gun.
ent-MobPirateT1MonkeyFireBomb = grenadier monkey
    .desc = At least it's not in the fridge. Will do anything for a paycheck in bananas. Carries a bundle of homemade incendiary bombs.
ent-MobPirateT1MonkeyEDagger = boarding monkey
    .desc = A pirate crew member who's been through more than one boarding action, but still works for bananas. Wields an energy dagger.
ent-MobPirateT1Flintlock = powder parrot
    .desc = A vox in the pirate crew, a veritable war parrot.
ent-MobPirateT1Hunter = goliath hunter
    .desc = A veteran salvager, wealthy enough to explore abandoned ruins and go boarding for the adrenaline and adventure.
ent-MobPirateT1HunterSmash = goliath smasher
    .desc = A veteran salvager, sturdy enough to swing a heavy crusher battleaxe with ease.
ent-MobPirateT1Knife = salvager boarder
    .desc = The first to climb through a breach. Rarely comes back, but sure makes a lot of noise.
ent-MobPirateT1ECutlass = veteran scavenger boarder
    .desc = Swings an energy cutlass with a distinctive Vwoom Vwoom sound, constantly showing off just how cool these Eeeeeenergy swords are.
ent-MobPirateT1Pickaxe = scavenger miner
    .desc = Armed with a trusty pickaxe and greed, every crew needs a simple fighter like this.
ent-MobPirateT1EPickaxe = veteran scavenger miner
    .desc = A marauder who has saved up enough coins to afford decent equipment.
ent-MobPirateT1Pistol = scavenger pistolero
    .desc = A low-ranking raider armed with a surplus weapon.
ent-MobPirateT1Medic = scavenger medic
    .desc = A field medic for the raiding party. Stays close to the group and supports the pirates with their aura. Definitely did NOT swear the Hippocratic Oath!
ent-MobPirateT1Mosin = scavenger marksman
    .desc = A rifleman with a weapon from the wars of antiquity. Loves quoting USSP regulations that no one has ever seen.
ent-MobPirateT1Rifle = veteran scavenger rifleman
    .desc = A hardened scavenger veteran who keeps their PPSh close and their bandolier even closer.
ent-MobPirateT1RifleAlt = veteran scavenger rifleman
    .desc = A hardened scavenger veteran with a cheap SMK-24.
ent-MobPirateT1ScrapRifle = scavenger automatic rifleman
    .desc = In a crew where everyone is armed with whatever they can find, they grabbed an automatic rifle. At least, it used to be one.
ent-MobPirateT1PKA = scavenger scrapper
    .desc = Proto-kinetic accelerator in hand, rum in their belly. That's how they earn their doubloons.
ent-MobPirateT1PlasmaCutter = veteran scavenger scrapper
    .desc = An experienced pirate salvager. With a plasma cutter, they can slice through shuttle hulls and make an entrance for the boarding party.
ent-MobPirateT1ScrapSMG = scavenger raider
    .desc = Loves shooting, hates aiming. Holds down the trigger until nothing around them is moving anymore. Armed with an improvised SMG.
ent-MobPirateT1SMG = veteran scavenger raider
    .desc = Loves shooting, hates aiming. Keeps pulling the trigger until nothing around him is moving. Armed with an ancient SMG.
ent-MobPirateT1BombardierFire = scavenger bombardier
    .desc = A thrill-seeker. Loves playing with fire, gunpowder, and welding fuel. Armed with a bombaga—a fearsome weapon of the tunnel-dwelling Grey Tide.
ent-MobPirateT1BombardierGlass = { ent-MobPirateT1BombardierFire }
    .desc = { ent-MobPirateT1BombardierFire.desc }
ent-MobPirateT1BombardierPipe = { ent-MobPirateT1BombardierFire }
    .desc = { ent-MobPirateT1BombardierFire.desc }
ent-MobPirateT1BorgAssault = assaultotron
    .desc = A former Syndicate assault borg. Rusty, dented, and reprogrammed by pirates. Still convinced that he's a weapon of mass persuasion.
ent-MobPirateT1BorgMining = digger
    .desc = A decommissioned mining borg, put back together as best as possible after an encounter with gibtonite. Wires stick out, panels are missing. Now it only digs up trouble.
ent-MobPirateT1BorgDerelict = scrapheap
    .desc = Once an ordinary borg without a specialization. After pirate training, it GOT A SPECIALIZATION. BEATING THINGS WITH A CROWBAR.
ent-MobPirateT2Grapeshot = shrapnel clunker
    .desc = Blasts everything to bits, turning things into Swiss cheese. Says that “shrapnel is an art form too.”
ent-MobPirateT2Cannoball = pirate cannoneer
    .desc = Loads cannons with explosive cannonballs—once one hits your sloop, there won't be anything left of it.
ent-MobPirateT2Cutlass = pirate boarder
    .desc = A freebooter in the boarding crew. Joined recently, but already makes full use of surprise and speed to seize his target.
ent-MobPirateT2ECutlass = veteran pirate boarder
    .desc = A member of the boarding crew. Uses surprise and st..—wait, he has an Eeeenergy Saber! Tremble, rats!
ent-MobPirateT2ECutlassTearGas = { ent-MobPirateT2ECutlass }
    .suffix = Tear Gas
    .desc = { ent-MobPirateT2ECutlass.desc }
ent-MobPirateT2ECutlassStinger = { ent-MobPirateT2ECutlass }
    .suffix = Traumatic
    .desc = { ent-MobPirateT2ECutlass.desc }
ent-MobPirateT2ECutlassFirebomb = { ent-MobPirateT2ECutlass }
    .suffix = Incendiary
    .desc = { ent-MobPirateT2ECutlass.desc }
ent-MobPirateT2Sledgehammer = pirate sledgehammerer
    .desc = A boarder armed with a sledgehammer capable of smashing through an airlock—or someone's head.
ent-MobPirateT2GauntletDrill = pirate driller
    .desc = Drills in the name of... drilling. No shuttle hull or mountain can withstand his drilling gauntlet.
ent-MobPirateT2Shotgun = pirate blunderbussman
    .desc = Knows his way around shotguns and carries a blunderbuss. Less shotgun, more handheld cannon. Fires anything that fits down the barrel.
ent-MobPirateT2Musket = pirate musketeer
    .desc = A pirate armed with an old-fashioned, large-caliber musket and bayonet.
ent-MobPirateT2MusketEMP = { ent-MobPirateT2Musket }
    .suffix = EMP
    .desc = { ent-MobPirateT2Musket.desc }
ent-MobPirateT2MusketFrag = { ent-MobPirateT2Musket }
    .suffix = Shrapnel
    .desc = { ent-MobPirateT2Musket.desc }
ent-MobPirateT2MusketPenetrator = { ent-MobPirateT2Musket }
    .suffix = Armor-Piercing
    .desc = { ent-MobPirateT2Musket.desc }
ent-MobPirateT2MachineCannon = pirate cannoneer
    .desc = A pirate with a belt-fed hand cannon... What?!
ent-MobPirateT2Mech = big Yark
    .desc = A heavy, ancient mech built for the harsh conditions of deep space. This brute is equipped with an integrated industrial mining drill.
ent-MobPirateT2Juggernaut = murmillo
    .desc = Clad in a heavy, ancient suit of armor. Slow, but extraordinarily tough.
ent-MobPirateT2DoubleFlintlock = pirate duelist
    .desc = Armed with a pair of old-fashioned flintlock pistols. Fires slowly, but hits hard.
ent-MobPirateT2DoubleRevolver = pirate gunslinger
    .desc = Uses two pirate revolvers. One revolver is good, but two are even better.
ent-MobPirateT2RevolverCutlass = pirate boatswain
    .desc = A seasoned pirate. Combines a shooter's accuracy with a boarder's ferocity. Prefers to shoot first, then hack apart whatever is left.
ent-MobPirateT3Revolver = bounty hunter
    .desc = A mercenary who has taken up the pirate flag. Quick hands, an even quicker trigger.
ent-MobPirateT3Grenadier = mercenary grenadier
    .desc = Covered in fireworks and bombs. Has never heard of safety regulations—or simply ignores them loudly.
ent-MobPirateT3Bola = mercenary pursuer
    .desc = A sponsored mercenary who hurls bolas. You won't be escaping this one.
ent-MobPirateT3Stun = mercenary stunner
    .desc = A freelancer who stuns you with a grenade first, then finishes the job.
ent-MobPirateT3Shield1984 = mercenary pistoleer
    .desc = A mercenary armed with a strobe shield and a quality pistol. You did bring sunglasses, right?
ent-MobPirateT3ShieldSMG = mercenary boarder
    .desc = A mercenary with a heavy ballistic shield. They can weather a hit and answer with a burst from their Scorpion.
ent-MobPirateT3DMR = mercenary marksman
    .desc = A fast rifle, accurate bursts, and a Syndicate stealth suit prototype. That's all you need to hunt down doubloons.
ent-MobPirateT3Infiltrator = veteran mercenary marksman
    .desc = An experienced marksman with a full suit of armor and stealth mode. Loves stealing food while remaining invisible.
ent-MobPirateT3Rifle = mercenary assault trooper
    .desc = Fast, aggressive, and reasonably accurate. That's usually enough.
ent-MobPirateT3Rifle2 = veteran mercenary assault trooper
    .desc = A freelancer in sturdy armor and jump boots.
ent-MobPirateT3L6 = veteran mercenary machine gunner
    .desc = Armed with a legendary L6 SAW; they must have gotten it on sale. Suppresses everything that moves.
ent-MobPirateT3SMG = mercenary raider
    .desc = Goes in first, shoots fast, and doesn't always hit the target. Armed with an old, heavy C-40 SMG.
ent-MobPirateT3Sniper = dragoon
    .desc = A freelancer with a Dragunov rifle. Once they got armor-piercing rounds, they became dangerous against any armor.
ent-MobPirateT3RPD = mercenary machine gunner
    .desc = Useful in an assault and dangerous everywhere else. Armed with an RPD-SH. Not as good as a SAW, but cheaper.
ent-MobPirateT3LaserSMG = salamander
    .desc = A mercenary armed with a laser submachine gun. Quickly floods the sector with fire and turns boarding into a light show.
ent-MobPirateT3LaserCannon = mamba
    .desc = A mercenary with a heavy plasma cannon. An expert at roasting you in your own juices.
ent-MobPirateT1Boss = rusty Fist
    .desc = An old veteran of the salvage crews, more metal than man.
ent-MobPirateT2Boss = captain Golden Bolt
    .desc = A legend of space, equal parts terrifying and drunk.
ent-MobPirateT3Boss = red Skull
    .desc = A heavy combat exosuit of the SSSP, Duranda variant. Slow, but relentless. Armed with an old heavy machine gun. Can dash, unleash fire, or vanish into smoke, all accompanied by a horrible laugh.
ent-MobPirateT3Tachanka = tachanka
    .desc = Machine gun! Mounted and loaded!
